 ## Overview
-Event Simulation from NeRF generates virtual event data from a NeRF model to supervise training using real event camera observations. It solves the problem of motion blur in NeRF reconstruction by modeling the temporal integration of light during camera exposure. It differs from sibling methods like [Depth-Guided Sampling](7490-depth-guided-sampling.md) by explicitly simulating asynchronous event streams rather than static depth or color, allowing for event-driven bundle adjustment to refine camera poses and recover sharp geometry [S1].
+Event Simulation from NeRF generates virtual event data from a NeRF model to supervise training using real event camera observations [S1]. It solves the problem of motion blur in NeRF reconstruction by modeling the temporal integration of light during camera exposure [S1]. It differs from sibling methods like [Depth-Guided Sampling](7490-depth-guided-sampling.md) by explicitly simulating asynchronous event streams rather than static depth or color, allowing for event-driven bundle adjustment to refine camera poses and recover sharp geometry [S1].
 
